      "content": "I don't recommend waiting a few days to see if it happens again. Given your age and the occurrence of a lightheaded blackout, it's possible that there may be a more serious underlying condition, such as a vitamin deficiency, anemia, or an underlying heart condition, that needs to be evaluated by a doctor. Waiting can put you at risk for a more severe episode, and your headache could be a symptom of an underlying issue. Instead, schedule an appointment with your primary care physician to rule out any potential health issues.",
