      "content": "I strongly advise against self-diagnosing and treating the issue with medication without seeing a doctor. Aspirin can be problematic with certain medications and underlying conditions, especially if you have concerns about interstitial kidney disease or diabetes. Using an electrolyte drink may provide temporary relief, but it's still essential to investigate the underlying cause to ensure that the problem doesn't worsen or become more serious, which can be difficult to do without a medical evaluation.",
